# If you want to see the complete list of every file Git is currently tracking, run:
# git ls-files
#
# And if you ever want to double-check whether a specific file inside <filepath> would be ignored if you created a new file there, run:
# git check-ignore -v <filepath>
# It is a test command that asks Git what it would do with a file path, even if that file does not exist yet on your computer. Git checks
# <filepath> against your .gitignore file from top to bottom and gives you one of two results:
# * Result 1: Blank output (No text returned)
#   * What it means: The file is NOT ignored. Your ! rules worked, and Git will track this file when you create it.
# * Result 2: Prints a file and line number (for example: .gitignore:2:*    <filepath>)
#   * What it means: The file IS ignored. It tells you the exact file (.gitignore), line number (2), and rule (*) that is blocking it.
#
# You can test which files Git will track before committing by running:
# git status --ignored -uall
#
# To stop Git from tracking a directory while keeping the files safe on your hard drive, remove it from Git's tracking index using
# --cached:
# git rm -r --cached <directory-name>/
#
#
# Pattern     What It Matches                      Effect Under a Top-Level *
# !folder/    The folder directory                 Unlocks the directory so Git can enter it, but
#             container only                       keeps its contents ignored.
# folder/*    All direct files and subfolders      Blocks everything inside folder so you can un-ignore
#             inside folder                        specific files below it.
# folder/*/   Direct subdirectories inside         Blocks all subfolders while leaving direct files inside
#             folder only                          folder untouched.
# !folder/*   All direct items inside folder       Includes all files and subfolders directly inside folder,
#             (1 level deep)                       without nested contents.
# !folder/**  Everything inside folder at          Includes every file and nested subdirectory while
#             all depths                           preserving the directory structure.
#
#
# Ignore everything.
*

#############################
# Application - Go and html #
#############################
!.dockerignore
!.editorconfig
!.gitignore
!Dockerfile-prod
!LICENSE
!README.md
#
!.github/
!.github/**
#
!src/
src/*
!src/go.mod
!src/go.sum
!src/main.go
!src/psql-clean.txt
!src/psql-list.txt
!src/upgrade-pg.sh
#
!src/concurrency/
!src/concurrency/**
#
!src/config/
src/config/*
!src/config/config.go
#
!src/databases/
!src/databases/**
#
!src/finances/
!src/finances/**
#
!src/mathutil/
src/mathutil/*
!src/mathutil/mathutil_test.go
!src/mathutil/mathutil.go
#
!src/renderer/
src/renderer/*
!src/renderer/render.go
#
!src/security/
src/security/*
!src/security/security.go
#
# Enter the directory.
!src/webfinances/
# Un-ignore everything directly inside src/webfinances (files and folders).
!src/webfinances/*
# Re-ignore ONLY directories inside src/webfinances (trailing slash matches folders only).
src/webfinances/*/
!src/webfinances/public/
!src/webfinances/public/**
!src/webfinances/templates/
!src/webfinances/templates/**
!src/webfinances/wfadmin/
!src/webfinances/wfadmin/**
!src/webfinances/wfbanking/
!src/webfinances/wfbanking/**
